.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For a bi-unitarily-invariant non-Hermitian matrix M = U \, \mathrm{diag}(s_1, \dots, s_n)\, V, built from independent Haar-random unitary matrices U, V and singular values s_i, the single ring theorem states that as n \to \infty the eigenvalues fill the annulus r_{\text{in}} \leq |z| \leq r_{\text{out}}, with radii fixed by only the first two moments of the limiting singular-value distribution:">

